  "summary": "Static keyword matches in CLI templates and tests with no traced installer-harm behavior",
  "details": "Package is a CLI shipping agent/skill templates and test fixtures. Static keyword matches occur in contexts that do not indicate installer harm: `dist/services/codex-pre-tool-hook-template.test.js` and `dist/services/codex-pre-tool-policy-template.js` contain example/forbidden-command strings (curl/wget/ping against placeholder hosts such as `evil.test` and `example.com`) used as policy test fixtures and guardrail denylist content, not as executed network calls. `Buffer.from(..., 'base64')` usages in `dist/services/global-codex-config.js` and `templates/.agents/skills/.../consumer-release-preparation.mjs` are standard encoding/decoding of configuration/text, not decode-and-eval. `templates/.agents/tools/runtime/api-mcp-runtime.mjs` contains ordinary HTTP GET/POST request handling in an MCP runtime template. No install/postinstall lifecycle hook, no top-level fetch-and-execute, no hardcoded attacker C2, no credential or environment scraping, and no exfiltration path is present.",
